## Abbreviations of company names, titles and addresses Zemberek lacks (TDK: San., Şti., Av.,
## Sok.), read as the word they stand for. Court decisions write them thousands of times
## (Tic. ve San. Ltd. Şti., Av. Ayşe Yılmaz), and without them San and Av counted as the
## nouns san "fame" and av "hunt", which then outranked sen in sana.
San [P:Abbrv; Pr:sanayi]
Şti [P:Abbrv; Pr:şirketi]
Av [P:Abbrv; Pr:avukat]
Sok [P:Abbrv; Pr:sokak]

## The same word as a circumflexed entry with the right attributes; Zemberek's bare copy
## without them accepted şahısı, mahlukadı.
şahıs [A:LastVowelDrop]
mahlukat [A:NoVoicing, ImplicitPlural]
mahlut [A:NoVoicing]
taallukat [A:NoVoicing]
serbesti [A:NoVoicing]
medlul [A:InverseHarmony]
nükul [A:InverseHarmony]
hulul [A:InverseHarmony]
mahlul [A:InverseHarmony]

## TDK: stok, -ku (Zemberek voices it: stoğu).
stok [A:NoVoicing]

## Institution names take their suffixes without an apostrophe (TDK: Danıştayın, Yargıtaya).
danıştay
yargıtay
sayıştay
karşıoy
## Legal terms.
nolu [P:Adj]
mucibince [P:Adv]
## Words that ended in the Arabic ayn take a vowel-initial suffix without a buffer
## (mercii, merciine, müdafiinin, tevdii); the pronunciation ending in ğ gives them that
## reading beside the buffered one.
merci [Pr:merciğ; Index:1]
mevki [Pr:mevkiğ; Index:1]
tevdi [Pr:tevdiğ; Index:1]
terfi [Pr:terfiğ; Index:1]
müdafi [Pr:müdafiğ; Index:1]
iştira [Pr:iştirağ; Index:1]
ziya [Pr:ziyağ; Index:1]
zıya [Pr:zıyağ; Ref:ziya]

## Phonology Zemberek lacks or infers wrongly (TDK): rehin, -hni; halefiyet, -ti; internet, -ti.
rehin [A:LastVowelDrop]
halefiyet [A:NoVoicing]
internet [A:NoVoicing]
## Attribute errors review 2 confirmed with TDK's suffix hints and corpus forms (MLEX2-04).
## avuç, -cu (avucu, not avcu); beyit, -yti; hısım, -smı; mehil, -hli; rızık, -zkı; emlak, -kı
## (back vowels, unvoiced); büyükşehir, -hri (a plain noun, not a compound with its own P3sg,
## so büyükşehirler reads); kalp, -bi in both senses; zabıt as the court writes it (zabtı 26,
## zabdı 0).
avuç [A:Voicing]
beyit [A:LastVowelDrop, NoVoicing]
hısım [A:LastVowelDrop]
mehil [A:LastVowelDrop]
rızık [A:LastVowelDrop, NoVoicing]
emlak [A:NoVoicing]
büyükşehir [A:LastVowelDrop]
kalp [A:Voicing, InverseHarmony]
kalp [A:Voicing, InverseHarmony; Index:1]
kalp [P:Adj; A:Voicing, InverseHarmony]
zabıt [A:LastVowelDrop, NoVoicing]
## Voicing Zemberek infers on words the court and RagTurk samples never voice (review 2's
## corpus flip audit: muhakematı 257 tokens and no voiced form; laptopun, aktivisti,
## tevfiki ...).
muhakemat [A:NoVoicing]
laptop [A:NoVoicing]
aktivist [A:NoVoicing]
sukut [A:NoVoicing]
tevfik [A:NoVoicing]
matufiyet [A:NoVoicing]
lejant [A:NoVoicing]
mamelek [A:NoVoicing]
tecvit [A:NoVoicing]
makat [A:NoVoicing]
memalik [A:NoVoicing]
## Variant spellings that take the front vowels of the standard ones (gayrimenkul, orijinal;
## şumul as TDK's şümul): gayrımenkulün 41 tokens, orjinalinde 17, şumulüne 6, none back.
gayrımenkul [A:InverseHarmony]
orjinal [A:InverseHarmony]
şumul [A:InverseHarmony]
## sulh takes either harmony in court text (sulhe 44 tokens, sulha 18, sulhun 22); TDK gives
## no hint (MLEX2-11).
sulh [A:NoVoicing; Index:1]
## Adjectives Zemberek lists only as a name or a noun: salih "fit, valid" (salih bir delil),
## ilâhî "divine".
salih [P:Adj]
ilâhî [P:Adj]

